1. c4 { [%eval 0.11] } 1... e5 { [%eval 0.14] } 2. g3! { [%eval 0.14] [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Avoids an early Bb4 } 2... Nf6 { [%eval 0.18] } (2... d5 3. cxd5 Qxd5 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Nc3 Qd8 6. Bg2 Nf6 7. O-O Bd6 8. d3 O-O 9. Bg5 h6 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. Rc1 Be6 12. Nd2 Qe7 13. Nc4) 3. Bg2 { [%eval 0.12] } 3... Nc6 { [%eval 0.36] } 4. Nc3 { [%eval 0.3] } { While there are tons of possible setups for Black, I will only cover the two major ones: Bb4 and Bc5. My recommendations against these lines lead to pretty similar positions. } 4... Bc5! { [%eval 0.21] } (4... Bb4! 5. Nd5 Bc5! (5... Nxd5?! 6. cxd5 Ne7 (6... Nd4?? 7. e3 Nf5 (7... Nb5 8. Qa4 { [%csl Rb4,Rb5][%cal Ra4b5,Ra4b4] }) 8. Qg4 { [%csl Rb4,Rf5,Rg7][%cal Rg4f5,Rg4g7,Rg4b4] }) 7. Nf3 d6?? (7... Ng6 8. h4) (7... Nxd5 8. Nxe5 Nf6 9. Nxf7 Kxf7 10. Qb3+ d5 11. Qxb4) 8. Qa4+! { [%csl Rb4,Re8][%cal Ra4b4,Ra4e8] }) (5... O-O 6. Nxb4 (6. a3 Bc5 (6... Bd6 7. e3 Nxd5 8. cxd5 Ne7 9. Ne2) 7. b4 Bd4 8. Rb1) 6... Nxb4 7. a3 Nc6 8. b4) 6. e3 { Sort of transposing back to the 4. Bc5 variation. } 6... O-O 7. Ne2 d6 8. O-O Nxd5 (8... Be6?? 9. d4 exd4 10. exd4 Bb6 11. Nxb6 axb6 12. d5) 9. cxd5 Ne7 10. d4 exd4 (10... Bb6 11. b3 f5 12. dxe5 dxe5 13. Bb2 { With pressure along both long diagonals }) 11. Nxd4) 5. e3! { [%eval 0.19] } { I have had success with both 5. Nf3 and 5. e3, but e3 seems to be the more straightforward one, with the clear plan to shut off the Bc5's diagonal. } { [%cal Gg1e2,Gd2d4] } (5. a3!? { [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Supporting e3, as black cannot rely on d5 as the Knight cannot go to b4 } { [%csl Bb4][%cal Ge2e3,Gg1e2,Ba3b4,Gc6b4] }) 5... d6 { [%eval 0.4] } (5... d5!? { Scores well for Black in practice, so I will go over this line a bit. } 6. cxd5 Nb4 { You can see it's not really a pawn sacrifice. Black will regain the pawn on d5 since White cannot allow Nd3+ } { [%csl Rd3,Re1][%cal Rd3e1] } 7. d4! exd4 8. exd4 Be7 (8... Bxd4?? 9. Qa4+! { Fork! }) 9. Nge2 { [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Don't try to hold the d5 pawn } 9... Nbxd5 (9... Bf5 10. Ng1 (10. O-O Qd7)) 10. O-O O-O 11. Nf4 c6 (11... Nxf4 12. Bxf4 Bd6 13. Be3) 12. Nfxd5 Nxd5 13. Nxd5 cxd5 14. Qb3 { With a fairly balanced position, but having the initiative. }) 6. Nge2 { [%eval 0.47] } 6... O-O { [%eval 0.43] } 7. O-O { [%eval 0.47] } 7... Bg4 { [%eval 0.84] } (7... Be6?? { This blunder occurs so often, even at the advanced level. Seems like normaly development, right? Wrong } 8. d4 { Fork coming right up }) (7... a6! 8. d4 exd4 (8... Ba7 9. b3 Bg4?! (9... exd4 { [%cal Ge2d4] }) 10. h3 { [%cal Gg3g4,Gg4h5,Gf2f4] } 10... Bf5 (10... Bxe2 11. Nxe2 exd4 12. exd4) 11. g4 Bd7 { [%cal Gf2f4,Ga1b1] }) 9. exd4 Ba7 10. h3! Re8 { [%cal Gb2b3,Ya2a3,Yb2b4] } (10... Bf5 11. Be3 { [%cal Ye3a7] } 11... Qd7? 12. g4 Bg6 13. d5 Ne7 14. Bxa7 Rxa7 { [%cal Gf2f4,Ge2g3] }) 11. a3 Rb8 12. b4 Bf5? 13. g4 Bg6 14. Bg5 h6 15. Bh4) 8. h3 { [%eval 1.12] } 8... Bh5? { [%eval 2.74] } { Mistake. Bd7 was best. } (8... Bxe2 9. Qxe2 Re8 10. b3 e4 11. Bb2) (8... Bd7 9. b3 Bb6 10. Kh2 Re8 11. f4 Nb4 12. Ba3 c5 13. Bxb7 Rb8 14. Bg2) 9. g4 { [%eval 2.62] } 9... Bg6 { [%eval 2.97] } 10. d4 { [%eval 2.93] } 10... Bb6 { [%eval 3.12] } 11. f4 { [%eval 2.65] } { Punishing black for developing the light squared bishop too early. It gets trapped on its own territory! } 11... exf4 { [%eval 3.3] } (11... h6 12. f5 Bh7 13. d5 Ne7 14. Ng3) 12. exf4 { [%eval 3.06] } 12... h6 { [%eval 3.14] } 13. f5 { [%eval 3.24] } 13... Bh7 { [%eval 3.34] } 14. Bf4! { [%eval 3.2] } 14... Re8 { [%eval 3.78] } 15. Bg3 { [%eval 3.61] } 15... Qe7 *


