1. c4 e6 2. Nf3 { [%cal Bg1f3] } 2... d5 { Here a Réti-Like position has been reached. This chapter is going to cover lines where Black plays e6 on the second move, followed by White's response of Knight to f3. } 3. g3 { White plays g3 in English fashion, preparing to develop the light-squared bishop. } 3... Nf6 { [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Neo-Catalan } 4. Bg2 { After White develops the Bishop to g2, Black usually plays 1 of 2 responses:
1. d takes c4
2. Bishop e7. } 4... dxc4 { [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Neo-Catalan Accepted } (4... Be7! { [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Declined } 5. O-O { [%anno "Mikae5", mikae5] Position has successfully transposed to the Reti Opening. } 5... O-O { After Bishop to e7, both players castle. } 6. b3 { White supports the pawn on c4 with b3. } 6... c5 { Black strikes with c5. } 7. Bb2 { White ignores this and plays Bishop to b2. } 7... Nc6 (7... d4 8. e3 Nc6 9. exd4 cxd4 10. Re1) 8. e3 { After Black develops the knight, White plays e3 to prepare d4. } 8... b6 9. Nc3 Bb7 { Both players develop their remaining minor pieces. } 10. cxd5 { White relieves some of the tension in the center. } 10... Nxd5 11. Nxd5 Qxd5 { A pair of knights is traded off. } 12. d4 Qf5 { White plays d4 and after Black plays Queen to f5 to get out of any nasty discoveries, White has a comfortable game here with ideas of a rook on d1 and c1 as well as playing Knight to e5. } { [%cal Gf3e5,Ga1c1,Gf1d1,Gd1d2,Gd1e2,Ge3e4,Gd4d5] }) 5. Qa4+ { White checks the King to win back the pawn. } 5... Nbd7 (5... c6 6. Qxc4 b5 7. Qc2 Bb7 8. O-O Be7 9. Nc3 O-O 10. Rd1) 6. Qxc4 c5 (6... a6 7. Qc2 c5 8. O-O) 7. O-O { White can simply castle here. } 7... b6 (7... a6 8. Qc2 b5 9. Nc3 Bb7 10. a4) 8. d4 { White can now push d4. } (8. b3 Bb7 9. Bb2 Be7 10. d3 O-O 11. Nbd2 Rc8 12. Rac1 Nb8 13. Rfd1 Nc6 14. Qc2) 8... Bb7 (8... cxd4? 9. Nxd4) 9. Nc3 { Both players continue development. } 9... Rc8 10. Rd1 { After Rook to d1 White has a good position and has ideas of b4 and a3 as well as developing the dark sqaured bishop to complete development. } { [%cal Ga2a3,Gb2b4,Gc1f4,Gc1g5,Ge2e4,Gf3e5,Gh2h4] } 10... Be7 (10... a6 11. dxc5 Bxc5 12. Qf4) 11. Bg5 *


